---
import BrooksideMark from './BrooksideMark.astro';
import { CHURCH } from '../data/church';

const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---

<footer class="bay rule rule--heavy foot">
	<div class="foot__brand">
		<BrooksideMark class="foot__mark" letter="#101010" cross="#E6534E" />
		<p class="foot__name">Brookside<br />Church of God</p>
	</div>
	<div class="foot__cols">
		<div>
			<h4>Find us</h4>
			<p>{CHURCH.street}<br />{CHURCH.locality}, Alabama {CHURCH.postalCode}</p>
			<a
				class="link"
				href={CHURCH.mapsUrl}
				target="_blank"
				rel="noopener"
			>Directions &rarr;</a>
		</div>
		<div>
			<h4>Reach us</h4>
			<p>
				<a href={CHURCH.phoneHref}>{CHURCH.phone}</a><br />
				<a href={CHURCH.emailHref}>{CHURCH.email}</a>
			</p>
		</div>
		<div>
			<h4>Gather</h4>
			{/*
				Each line is nowrap: the column is narrow enough that "Morning
				Worship 10:45 AM" broke before the meridiem on every page, leaving a
				line reading just "AM". The times are also the church's own names for
				these gatherings, not "Sunday service" and "Bible study".
			*/}
			<p class="foot__times">
				<span>Sunday School 9:45 AM</span>
				<span>Morning Worship 10:45 AM</span>
				<span>Wednesday Classes 6:30 PM</span>
			</p>
		</div>
		{/*
			Explore, added 2026-08-21. Both pages are reachable from the body of the
			site as well (the declaration from /about, Knowing Christ from Home and
			the foot of /watch), but neither is in the main nav and neither should
			be: that was cut from seven items to five on purpose, and a doctrinal
			statement is not a top-level destination. The footer is how a reference
			document stays findable without spending a nav slot.

			`.foot__cols` is `auto-fit, minmax(150px, 1fr)`, so this fifth column
			reflows on its own and needs no grid change. It lands 4 + 1 at 1440,
			with Follow alone on the second row.

			DO NOT try to squeeze five onto one row. Measured at 1440: the grid is
			842px with a 40px gap, and the Gather column's widest nowrap string
			("Morning Worship 10:45 AM") needs 181px. Five columns in 842px gives
			136px even at ZERO gap, so it cannot fit, and narrowing the columns
			re-breaks the exact wrap those nowrap spans were added to fix — the one
			that left a line reading just "AM". The wrap is forced arithmetic, not
			an oversight.

			Follow is the deliberate orphan: Gather and Explore are both site
			content and belong together on the first row, and Follow is external
			links, so it is the one that loses least by dropping down.
		*/}
		<div>
			<h4>Explore</h4>
			<p>
				<a href="/what-we-believe/">What we believe</a><br />
				<a href="/knowing-christ/">Knowing Christ</a>
			</p>
		</div>
		<div>
			<h4>Follow</h4>
			<p>
				<a href="https://facebook.com/BrooksideChurchofGod" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Facebook</a><br />
				<a href="https://instagram.com/brooksidechurchofgod" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Instagram</a><br />
				<!-- The channel's own canonical handle. The raw UC… channel ID still
				     works and is what the /watch embed needs, but this is the URL to
				     show a human. -->
				<a href="https://www.youtube.com/@brooksidechurchofgod" target="_blank" rel="noopener">YouTube</a>
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
	<p class="foot__legal">&copy; {year} Brookside Church of God</p>
</footer>
